<div id="guideModal" class="modal-backdrop" hidden><section class="modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="guideTitle"><div class="modal-head"><h2 id="guideTitle">OMG scoring &amp; interpretation guide</h2><button class="btn small" data-close-modal="guideModal" type="button">Close ✕</button></div><p class="subtext">Met and Transformational are positive. Not Met is a valid negative rating. Blank and N/A cells are excluded from scoring.</p><div class="guide-grid"><div class="guide-box"><h3>01 · Ownership</h3><p><b>Fix, Guide &amp; Tidy Up</b></p><p>Own the path forward, make next steps clear, explain escalations transparently, and provide a clean wrap-up.</p><p>Do not imply that support can force or speed up external processes.</p></div><div class="guide-box"><h3>02 · Lower Effort</h3><p><b>Research &amp; Align</b></p><p>Use available history, avoid repetition, eliminate unnecessary steps, and provide a direct path.</p><p>Reasonable, clearly explained merchant actions are not automatically a failure.</p></div><div class="guide-box"><h3>03 · Genuine Empathy</h3><p><b>Connect First</b></p><p>Acknowledge the specific situation and business impact, pair human care with action, and use an authentic tone.</p><p>Negative sentiment alone does not make empathy Not Met; generic phrases alone do not justify Transformational.</p></div></div><div class="note-box"><b>Rates:</b> Positive = (Met + Transformational) / (Met + Not Met + Transformational). Overall QA pools positive ratings across all three signals. Intervened = Yes / (Yes + No); recorded-Yes / eligible is also shown. Resolution reconciles every header named Resolution. Qualified Yes/No answers retain their reason; contradictions are excluded. Yes, No in one cell is conflicting. Intervention uses the configured live-audit types. Signal scope and all excluded response counts appear in the detail views.</div><div class="note-box"><b>Interpretation:</b> Driver shares use classified audits, not all merchant contacts. Counts, per-100-audit frequency and calendar-day averages are descriptive. Intervention frequency does not prove effectiveness. Recommendations are proposed actions, not confirmed coaching completion. The 80% Smiley and 70% Sentiment targets cannot be assessed from these signal ratings.</div><p class="section-note">Reporting uses the Date column in the spreadsheet timezone. Any inclusive range is supported. Weeks run Sunday–Saturday and use WBMMDD. KPI day movements compare the selected end date with the preceding date. KPI week movements compare Sunday through that end date with the same elapsed days one week earlier. These supporting windows can extend outside the main date selection. Presentation mode hides staff controls and the ticket log from the visible executive view; it is not a separate access-control role.</p></section></div>
